%I A395595 #39 Aug 19 2026 16:18:32
%S A395595 1,1,2,4,36,963,375718
%N A395595 Number of orbits of rowmotion on the order ideals of the Boolean lattice B_n.
%C A395595 Let B_n be the poset of subsets of [n], ordered by inclusion. For an order ideal I of B_n, rowmotion sends I to the order ideal generated by the minimal elements of B_n \ I. Then a(n) is the number of cycles of this permutation.
%C A395595 If A is an antichain and I=down(A), rowmotion induces the antichain map G(A)=min(B_n \ down(A)). This is the inverse of the Brouwer-Schrijver map F(A)=max(B_n \ up(A)), so the two permutations have the same cycles.
%C A395595 If c_n(k) is the number of cycles of length k, then Sum_{k>=1} k*c_n(k) = A000372(n). For n=6 the full orbit-length histogram has 79 nonzero entries, its largest length is 1032, Sum c_6(k) = 375718, and Sum k*c_6(k) = 7828354.
%C A395595 The terms through n=6 were obtained by exhaustive enumeration. Two independent C++20 implementations, using respectively the minimal-complement definition and reverse-linear-extension toggles, give identical successor maps and orbit histograms.
%H A395595 A. E. Brouwer and A. Schrijver, <a href="https://ir.cwi.nl/pub/6948/6948D.pdf">On the period of an operator, defined on antichains</a>, report ZW 24/74 (1974).
%H A395595 P. J. Cameron and D. G. Fon-Der-Flaass, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/0195-6698(95)90036-5">Orbits of antichains revisited</a>, European Journal of Combinatorics 16 (1995), 545-554.
%H A395595 M. Deza and K. Fukuda, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4613-8994-1_7">Loops of clutters</a>, in Coding Theory and Design Theory, Part I (1990), 72-92.
%F A395595 If c_n(k) is the number of rowmotion cycles of length k, then a(n) = Sum_{k>=1} c_n(k) and Sum_{k>=1} k*c_n(k) = A000372(n).
%e A395595 The 6 ideals of B_2 form one rowmotion cycle of length 2 and one cycle of length 4, so a(2) = 2.
%Y A395595 Cf. A000372 (number of order ideals/antichains of B_n), A269699 (order ideals of B_n by cardinality), A305716 (order of rowmotion on divisor lattices), A348260 (a different action: S_n-orbits of maximal antichains), and A369313 (rowmotion on interval-closed subsets of B_n).
%K A395595 nonn,hard,more,new
